mm/page_alloc: disable watermark_boost under CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS

On UML-NT (CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS) with a 128 MiB single-zone memory pool and
no swap or background kswapd compaction, guest 64 KiB physical runs are
allocated with GFP_KERNEL (MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE). When order-0 pagecache
allocations (GFP_HIGHUSER_MOVABLE) fall back to MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE
pageblocks, boost_watermark() adds up to 4096 KiB to
zone->watermark_boost, raising the effective min watermark from 1344 KiB
to 5440 KiB and triggering false OOM kills when >5 MiB of RAM is free.

Disable watermark_boost_factor under CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS, matching upstream
boost_watermark()'s small-zone exemption rationale.

Signed-off-by: uml-nt agent <droid@factory.ai>
---
 a/mm/page_alloc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -301,7 +301,11 @@ const char * const migratetype_names[MIGRATE_TYPES] = {
 
 int min_free_kbytes = 1024;
 int user_min_free_kbytes = -1;
+#ifdef CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS
+static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly;
+#else
 static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly = 15000;
+#endif
 static int watermark_scale_factor = 10;
 int defrag_mode;
 
